    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470-a5">

                <pb facs="1538" n="1380" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1380"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Bergholz to Minister Leishman</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Beirut, Syria</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your telegram
                    of the 18th instant as follows:<anchor n="a" xml:id="d470-f1"/></p>
                <p>The receipt of the instructions is admitted by the director.</p>
                <p>I need not tell you that the receipt of your two telegrams caused much rejoicing
                    among the American colony, which is loud in expressing its great satisfaction at
                    the recognition of these institutions by the Porte.</p>
                <p>May I be permitted to add my congratulations upon the success which has crowned
                    your efforts?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leo Bergholz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
